WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.820
The first film grew DNA inside bacteria.

2
00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:06.740
Now two PCR tubes end equally bright.

3
00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:09.360
Did they start with the same amount?

4
00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:12.780
The answer hides in how the signal grew.

5
00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:17.020
Watch a bounded target become a curve that can be read.

6
00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:26.490
PCR starts with template DNA, primers, nucleotides, and heat-stable polymerase.

7
00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:29.870
A yellow primer binds each grey strand.

8
00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:33.310
Their 3' ends point into the target.

9
00:00:34.730 --> 00:00:36.530
Polymerase extends from those ends.

10
00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:41.270
Primer placement sets the candidate boundaries for amplification.

11
00:00:42.633 --> 00:00:44.773
Heating separates template strands.

12
00:00:46.133 --> 00:00:48.073
Cooling lets each primer pair with its site.

13
00:00:49.473 --> 00:00:53.733
Polymerase extends each primer, building blue DNA along grey template.

14
00:00:55.053 --> 00:00:58.073
Repeat the cycle, and earlier products become templates.

15
00:00:59.373 --> 00:01:04.273
Like a photocopier whose copies can be copied, the bounded target branches into a

16
00:01:04.273 --> 00:01:05.273
growing family.

17
00:01:06.133 --> 00:01:10.893
During ideal early cycles, each completed target can seed another copy.

18
00:01:12.493 --> 00:01:15.513
Product can double every cycle, bending the graph upward.

19
00:01:16.813 --> 00:01:21.433
The blue curve is computed from starting amount times two raised to cycle number.

20
00:01:22.773 --> 00:01:24.953
Real reactions follow this only early.

21
00:01:26.083 --> 00:01:30.103
As product accumulates, amplification slows toward a plateau.

22
00:01:31.563 --> 00:01:34.423
Different starting amounts can finish at similar levels.

23
00:01:35.823 --> 00:01:38.823
Endpoint brightness loses how each reaction arrived there.

24
00:01:40.143 --> 00:01:45.123
Real-time PCR preserves that history by measuring fluorescence throughout the run,

25
00:01:45.623 --> 00:01:47.683
while early curves remain separated.

26
00:01:48.783 --> 00:01:51.263
A green threshold crosses both curves.

27
00:01:52.503 --> 00:01:55.983
One curve reaches it earlier, although both endpoints look alike.

28
00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:59.183
Which reaction began with more target?

29
00:02:00.543 --> 00:02:03.903
Think about how many rounds each needed to reach the same fluorescence.

30
00:02:10.017 --> 00:02:13.077
The earlier crossing came from more starting target.

31
00:02:14.377 --> 00:02:17.937
That reaction needed fewer rounds to reach the shared threshold.

32
00:02:19.277 --> 00:02:22.297
The crossing is the threshold cycle, written Ct.

33
00:02:23.617 --> 00:02:29.417
With matched, near-perfect efficiency, an earlier Ct means more starting template.

34
00:02:30.637 --> 00:02:32.837
The plateau cannot support that inference.

35
00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:37.970
Real-time quantitative PCR watches DNA accumulate.

36
00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:41.930
Reverse-transcription PCR starts differently.

37
00:02:43.570 --> 00:02:49.390
Reverse transcriptase copies RNA into complementary DNA, which PCR can amplify.

38
00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:53.270
Combining the steps measures an RNA target.

39
00:02:54.470 --> 00:02:58.530
The fluorescence still reports amplified DNA, not RNA directly.

40
00:02:59.733 --> 00:03:03.293
A curve is evidence only within a controlled comparison.

41
00:03:04.713 --> 00:03:07.513
A tube with no template can expose contamination.

42
00:03:09.093 --> 00:03:14.053
For RNA, a tube without reverse transcriptase can expose genomic DNA.

43
00:03:15.533 --> 00:03:17.653
A known positive shows the assay works.

44
00:03:19.393 --> 00:03:22.453
Controls turn a glowing curve into an interpretable result.

45
00:03:23.517 --> 00:03:27.637
The early rising curve preserves information about starting amount.

46
00:03:28.997 --> 00:03:31.917
The endpoint mostly shows that product accumulated.

47
00:03:33.317 --> 00:03:37.897
Read the crossing under stated assumptions, then challenge the signal with controls.

48
00:03:39.277 --> 00:03:43.057
The useful measurement is when the curve arrives, not how bright it ends.
